cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ContextSafe, please cite it as below."
title: "ContextSafe — offline synthetic fixture validator and deterministic evaluator for transgender and nonbinary patient-safety release gating"
abstract: >-
  A clinically and community-governed release-gate plan, with a bounded offline
  implementation slice: strict versioned schemas for synthetic patient cases and
  observations, a fail-closed deterministic evaluator where missing or ambiguous
  evidence is indeterminate, unsigned governance-contract compilation, and a
  recoverable synthetic-evidence store producing hash-covered JSON receipts.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chelsea
    family-names: Kelly-Reif
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/contextsafe"
keywords:
  - patient-safety
  - transgender-health
  - health-informatics
  - hl7-fhir
  - synthetic-data
  - release-gating
  - deterministic-evaluation
# `version` and `date-released` name the first release, staged here rather than
# after the fact: `.github/workflows/release.yml` fires on the tag and re-verifies
# the tagged commit, so everything the release asserts has to be true in the commit
# the tag points at. The release exists once `v0.1.0` is pushed; if that happens on
# a different day, this date and the `## [0.1.0]` heading in CHANGELOG.md move
# together. The pipeline builds an sdist and a wheel and deliberately has no
# publish or sign step — there is no distribution channel, and a citable version is
# not a claim of clinical approval. See docs/PUBLICATION-READINESS.md.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-02
